",\"args\":{\"query\":\"\\\"\\\\\\\"RPF8\\\\\\\" rdr2 archive format specification OR header\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching RPF8 format\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search RPF8 format\\\"\"}}]}\n37: {\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-24T22:56:10Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-24T17:56:10-05:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T17:56:15-05:00\\nThe search for \\\"\\\"RPF8\\\" rdr2 archive format specification OR header\\\" returned the following summary:\\nThe **RPF8** archive format is a proprietary package format utilized by Rockstar Games for **Red Dead Redemption 2 (RDR2)** on PC (running on the RAGE engine)[1][2]. It builds directly upon the architecture of GTA V’s **RPF7** format[3] while introducing specific structural shifts—most notably replacing plain text filename strings in the table of contents with **hash-based keys**[4].\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. General Header Structure (First 16 Bytes)\\nLike preceding RAGE package formats (RPF7), the file begins with a 16-byte header consisting of four little-endian 32-bit unsigned integers (`uint32`)[4]:\\n\\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Description / Value |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `0x00` | 4 bytes | **Magic** | `RPF8` (`0x38465052` little-endian)[1][5] |\\n| `0x04` | 4 bytes | **Entry Count** | Total number of file/directory entries contained in the archive table of contents. |\\n| `0x08` | 4 bytes | **Names Length / Table Size** | Length or data size allocated for the metadata/nametables. |\\n| `0x0c` | 4 bytes | **Encryption Type** | Indicates encryption mode flags (e.g., `OPEN`, `AES`, `NG`)[4]. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Core Differences from RPF7 (GTA V)\\nWhile RPF7 and RPF8 share a very similar node-based virtual file system layout (utilizing 16-byte Table of Contents entries split into directories, binary files, and resource files)[6], RPF8 diverges significantly in how it handles file identity:\\n\\n* **No Filename String Blob:** Unlike RPF7—which embeds a raw string block containing paths and file names right after the TOC entries—RPF8 entries are **keyed entirely by hashes** instead of embedded filenames[4]. \\n* **External Nametables:** Because file paths are hashed directly into identifiers within the binary structure, human-readable file names are absent from the retail archives themselves. Modern open-source toolchains (`rage-cli`, `rdr2x`) recover\\n<truncated 1672 bytes>\\n7glryQD4A9WlcIjCC445_Ywe_NVJGbdT3J9CY6mRCj2_XB_YrCyQO7rgCdvceVGYQ68NNAZU1rhd-Xb-OZpYDt9x85xxTGV0BEn3NrUnViIbKdT1S3MR6VzuT1mmFklgDPmjZ1W4CPwzKqkXZsqbYWRPTFSJ97H5SPCexk=)\\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzSRU-VXzHEYHN0dWpL4AvWRzxJvsKx2WBRRNjUJBdTYJrgel7Xpn64aMAOZUNSq57u4K0TjafdC-ZKlpU55SUZeoCRXSepuzi6tYF5x9LE0fVKISBtNCeFATtc0DpWXqfPTz_Mc2myugpR5Ojvw2lSKHmc9xk_Y1JInpLsCzXW5E=)\\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzSRU-VXzHEYHN0dWpL4AvWRzxJvsKx2WBRRNjUJBdTYJrgel7Xpn64aMAOZUNSq57u4K0TjafdC-ZKlpU55SUZeoCRXSepuzi6tYF5x9LE0fVKISBtNCeFATtc0DpWXqfPTz_Mc2myugpR5Ojvw2lSKHmc9xk_Y1JInpLsCzXW5E=)\\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzSRU-VXzHEYHN0dWpL4AvWRzxJvsKx2WBRRNjUJBdTYJrgel7Xpn64aMAOZUNSq57u4K0TjafdC-ZKlpU55SUZeoCRXSepuzi6tYF5x9LE0fVKISBtNCeFATtc0DpWXqfPTz_Mc2myugpR5Ojvw2lSKHmc9xk_Y1JInpLsCzXW5E=)\\n[7] [nexusmods.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGHp6MZv5k3UJ5r9Pi2QyrJ0MK97xDSx4Oln-lOUAPT2UGeXuU1ZdXFr4nT3dMcmCbLFep4Cdzy2rz74jn6vPnntOzKQ9QOM3VYLOtTI0wEjO0uYI6IKGnTIZdodTyKCmQebIJ5ZhtZBN8AwPfZ)\\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCt_XGRV3I2I8KLcjkOq4L91FzfBxZO8DzCo9SbL5Ysa_lKX1Fiq3tTVsx2giqG42sjJZ8adkCak5qvRkcWvDgVDzoEkFQ-Gk96-f49wQ7t5LX_HTNUkIs)\\n[9] [file-extension.info](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFuiqKDSGgEnRMAM8v5gOSF7NvAPEdJ