r builds)[2][3].\\n\\n### 2. Mission Flows, `story000`, and Internal Nomenclature\\nIn Rockstar Games' proprietary RAGE engine development structure, internal mission scripts and debug strings are typically categorized systematically:\\n* **`story000` / Prologue files:** In leaked debugging nomenclature, text strings, global states, and master flow scripts often begin with `story000` or foundational index tags to dictate the initialization of the game's script logic, character switching parameters, and cutscene triggers.\\n* **Mission Flow & Lists:** Leaked internal debugging trees and development text assets gave data-miners an early look at how chapters transition. In these developer documents, missions are categorized by internal codenames before receiving final retail titles. \\n\\n### 3. Leaks vs. The Final Release\\nWhile early data-miners combed through Cyberleek's dumps looking for mission flow lines, debug names, and placeholder scripts (`story000`, etc.), the actual game launched with a structured campaign consisting of roughly 91 main story missions spanning 5 distinct chapters featuring protagonists Jason and Lu\\n<truncated 241 bytes>\\nl underworld and epilogue sequences[4][7].\\n\\nSources:\\n[1] [mmoexp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHNX7TtsWLQnK8jPacTJB6qX3GRsgslo5nnhRZBB7LLU0escjN4jMagTpZxZWUVCMt5asjaujaWuPailDRBWNKe_t2DShVRnjTc-0el_TJ2WGiCokhgc22ZyByEh_lwQTI9k1x60hE-Tb9xnSwsk95cPNaC3HeCHY4tU9EFSJb8FQd1zTOoEmQYN0ZF7q8JxPqoGkyJjE5CsZvJJ34dSTzQJN0i)\\n[2] [gamesindustry.biz](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE6pCr5rWPTCjyQyk1-4510ScFeLoinNMwNYEZ4MxKg1n3xAZZ5EkNCZHE4lCEwTRnGjDc28VF9rivuV9kJvrvc5-k3TrOAreDePK9m0wt8d8oIyG6xyQnYpofAeMNcQFzs5djzuvNqS4nZD_cn-t5rGlqi05Z1ffUcf6v_XD7vlZgIqY7p9eI7swKxzZIu2Qy04czHmdsD5jA=)\\n[3] [ign.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFyAdPIspshzGdRgr73ZK6KCl4cmvrrNKajY3AN8fKOWJQ1Y69KX88McOkycnnt7-SL0VMavpNmTCwmH